This C program interfaces with a Melexis MLX91211 Triaxis Current Sensor through an MCP3008 ADC on SPI0 on a Raspberry Pi 4 Model B. It reads the current every second, converts the ADC reading to amperes, logs the data to a file, and implements error handling and graceful termination by catching SIGINT and SIGTERM. If the measured current exceeds 10.0 A, it drives GPIO17 low to disable the motor, logs the over-current event, waits one second, then drives GPIO17 high to re-enable the motor.

