This C program sets up a Raspberry Pi 3 Model B+ to read the analog output of a Honeywell MICROceL MCO‑S4 CO sensor through an MCP3008 ADC on SPI0. It continuously samples channel 0 once per second, logs the timestamp and voltage to a file named `co_log.txt`, and drives a GPIO pin to indicate when the measured voltage exceeds 2.5 V. The program handles errors, retries SPI transfers, and turns off the alarm pin for safety. It also handles SIGINT and SIGTERM signals to close resources and exit gracefully.

