This C program continuously reads temperature and pressure data from a TDK ICP-10125 I2C sensor attached to I2C bus 1, issuing the documented high-precision measurement command, waiting for the conversion, and then reading the 6-byte result (pressure MSB/LSB, temperature MSB/LSB, CRC bytes) and applying the official ICP-10125 calibration formulas to convert the raw ADC values to degrees Celsius and pascals. The program samples every 5 seconds, logs each timestamped reading to a file named environmental_data.csv, displays the values on the console for real-time monitoring, checks the result of every I2C system call (open, ioctl, write, read) and, on any sensor-absent or bus-error condition, logs the error and retries after 5 seconds, and finally handles graceful shutdown by catching SIGINT and SIGTERM, closing both the I2C file descriptor and the CSV log file before exiting.

