This C program continuously monitors soil moisture using a Keyes KY-036 analog sensor connected to an MCP3008 10-bit SPI ADC on a Raspberry Pi 3 Model B+. It reads the sensor once per second by default, but the interval can be overridden by a numeric argument passed as `argv[1]`. The program logs each reading to a file named `soil_moisture.log` with an ISO-8601 timestamp, the raw 10-bit ADC value, and the calculated moisture percentage. It handles errors and signals gracefully, ensuring that the SPI device and log file are properly closed before exiting.

