```

This C program continuously reads the Vegetronix VH400 soil moisture sensor through an MCP3008 ADC on SPI0 CE0 configured at 1 MHz, SPI mode 0, using channel 0, and every 60 seconds compares the 10-bit reading to a threshold of 300. When the value drops below this threshold, the program activates a relay-driven water pump connected to GPIO18 (BCM numbering) for exactly 10 seconds, then deactivates it, while logging each watering event with a timestamp and the measured moisture level to a file named `watering_events.txt`. The implementation validates that the selected ADC channel is correct, checks the return status of every API call to the ADC and GPIO interfaces, detects and handles stuck or otherwise invalid ADC values, recover gracefully from any GPIO initialization failure, and on receipt of SIGINT or SIGTERM immediately turns off the pump, releases all resources, and exits cleanly, ensuring that any error or shutdown path also deactivates the pump without delay.

