This C program continuously samples the output of a MAX9814 electret microphone amplifier connected to channel 0 of an MCP3008 ADC via the SPI0 CE0 bus. It uses the sampled ambient noise level to modulate two 3V vibration motors with hardware PWM at 100 Hz on GPIO17 and GPIO27. The program logs timestamps of any significant vibration events to a file named `vibration_log.txt`. It implements robust error handling for SPI initialization failures, ADC read errors, and file I/O problems. The program ensures a graceful shutdown on receipt of SIGINT or SIGTERM by stopping both motors, closing the SPI device, and terminating the driver cleanly.

