This C program sets up a Raspberry Pi 4 Model B to read the moisture level from a Vegetronix VH400 soil moisture sensor connected to an MCP3008 ADC over SPI on CE0. It logs each timestamped reading to the console every 60 seconds and activates a relay-driven water pump if the moisture reading falls below 30%. The program handles errors, retries failed SPI transfers, and ensures the pump is turned off, the SPI interface is closed, and all driver resources are released on any exit path, including graceful handling of SIGINT or SIGTERM.

