This C program continuously monitors a GP2Y0A21YK0F IR distance sensor connected through an MCP3008 ADC on SPI0 using chip-enable CE0 and channel 0 at a 1 MHz bus speed. It polls the sensor every 100 ms, and when the measured distance falls below 20 cm, it energizes a relay on GPIO17 (BCM numbering, active‑high) to simulate a door opening, then enforces a 1 s debounce delay before further detection, while logging each detection event with a timestamp to a file named door_events.log. The implementation includes robust error handling for all GPIO, SPI, and file I/O operations, correctly handles cases where the sensor is absent or the bus reports errors, and ensures that all resources are cleanly released on every exit path, including handling a SIGINT signal.

