This C program reads the voltage from an MQ-3 alcohol sensor through an MCP3008 ADC on SPI0 CE0 (GPIO8) using channel 0 in single-ended mode at 1 MHz, SPI mode 0 with 8-bit words, samples the sensor once every second, classifies the reading into three ranges, and appends each timestamped measurement to a file named alcohol_log.txt using ISO 8601 UTC timestamps. It handles ADC read errors by validating each SPI transfer, retrying a failed read up to three times with a 100 ms delay before logging an error, detects a sensor-absent condition when the ADC consistently returns 0 or 1023 and reports it, checks every system call return value and emits descriptive error messages, and on receipt of SIGINT or SIGTERM performs a graceful shutdown that closes the log file, releases all file descriptors and GPIO resources.

