This C program sets up a Raspberry Pi Zero W to sample an analog audio signal from an ADMP401 MEMS microphone connected to an MCP3008 10-bit SPI ADC. It uses the SPI bus at `/dev/spidev0.0` with mode 0, 8 bits per word, and a maximum clock of 1 MHz. The chip-select line is manually toggled on GPIO 8, and the program acquires a raw ADC reading at a fixed 1000 Hz rate, writing each sample to a file named `audio_log.txt` with a timestamp. The program handles signals to release resources and gracefully exit.

