This C program uses the `libgpiod` library to interact with the GPIO pins on a Raspberry Pi 3 Model B+. It reads the digital states of three Texas Instruments DRV5055VA Hall-effect sensors connected to GPIO4, GPIO17, and GPIO27, simulates an ADC by interpreting HIGH as 3.3V and LOW as 0.0V, converts each state to a magnetic field strength value, and logs the three computed values in millitesla to a file named `magnetic_log.txt`. The program includes robust error handling for GPIO access and file I/O, prints a warning to stderr whenever any computed magnetic field falls outside the range -100mT to +100mT, skips the logging for that iteration if any GPIO read fails, and handles SIGINT (Ctrl-C) to perform a graceful shutdown that releases all driver resources properly.

