This C program initializes a Raspberry Pi 5 to read the digital output of a Keyes KY-026 flame sensor module connected to GPIO pin 17. It uses the `libgpiod` library to handle GPIO operations, including setting up the line for input with a pull-down resistor. The program logs each reading to a CSV file named `flame_events.log` with columns for timestamp, pin, and state. It also prints an alarm message to stderr whenever the sensor reports a HIGH state. The program handles errors and cleans up all GPIO resources on normal termination and when receiving SIGINT or SIGTERM.

