This C program reads moisture from three DFRobot Soil Moisture Sensor v2.0 analog resistive sensors connected to an MCP3008 ADC via the SPI bus on CE0, mode 0 at 1 MHz, with the sensors wired to MCP3008 channels 0, 1, and 2. It sleeps for 60 seconds between cycles, appends each reading to a file named `soil_data.txt` in the format "YYYY-MM-DD HH:MM:SS" with one line per sensor per cycle, prints an error and exits with code 1 if any of the required driver functions fail, prints an error and continues if an ADC value is invalid, and on receipt of SIGINT closes the SPI interface, closes the log file, terminates the driver, and prints a goodbye message, ensuring proper resource cleanup on all exit paths while using only the provided driver functions.

