This C program uses the `libgpiod` library to monitor two Omron B5W-DB01 diffuse reflective proximity sensors connected via GPIO on a Raspberry Pi 5. It implements a debounce routine to read each sensor five times spaced 2ms apart, uses the majority value to determine the sensor state, logs the state once per second to the console, checks for an alert when both sensors report object presence simultaneously, and handles errors and exits gracefully. The program also installs a SIGINT handler to release all GPIO resources on termination.

