This code sets up a Raspberry Pi 3 Model B+ to read soil moisture from a YL-69 sensor connected to an MCP3008 ADC on SPI channel 0, CE0, operating at a 1 MHz baud rate. It samples every 60 seconds, converts the raw ADC value to a moisture percentage, logs each reading with a timestamp to a file named `soil_moisture_log.csv`, and prints the same line to the console. The program handles errors by checking driver library initialization, SPI open, SPI transfer, and file open, printing an error and retrying on SPI transfer failure without exiting, printing an error and continuing on file open failure, and ensures proper cleanup on SIGINT by using a volatile sig_atomic_t flag in a signal_handler that closes the SPI handle, terminates the driver library, and exits cleanly. All resources are released on error paths such as terminating the driver library before returning if SPI open fails.

