This C program captures grayscale images from an Arducam OV5647 CSI camera module using the CSI bus device supplied as a command-line argument. It configures the camera for an 8-bit grayscale format, sets up memory-mapped streaming with a single buffer, and continuously dequeues frames, handling the EAGAIN condition by using select() with a 2-second timeout. Each frame is saved as a sequential .pgm file named image_0001.pgm, image_0002.pgm, and so on. The program includes robust error handling for every open(), ioctl(), mmap(), fwrite(), and close() call, printing strerror(errno) on failure, gracefully handles EAGAIN when dequeuing buffers, and cleanly releases all resources on every exit path. It also installs signal handlers for SIGINT and SIGTERM that stop streaming and safely unmap the buffers, while never using the C++ API of libcamera.

