This C program uses the `libgpiod` library to control a Raspberry Pi camera pan-tilt mount using the GPIO software PWM bus and four active-low push-buttons with internal pull-ups. The program initializes both servos to the mid-position value 75, adjusts the corresponding axis by ±5 while clamping the position to the range 25–125, and polls the button states every 50 ms. It handles any request failures and on receipt of SIGINT cleanly releases all allocated resources.

