This C program uses the `libgpiod` library to monitor the HC-SR501 PIR sensor on GPIO17. It implements a 50ms debounce by waiting for a falling edge with a timeout. Upon a valid motion event, it captures an image using the `raspistill` command and logs the capture and any errors to `/home/pi/motion_capture.log`. The program handles SIGINT and SIGTERM by releasing all driver library resources and closing file descriptors.

