This C program continuously polls an E18-D50NK IR proximity sensor connected to GPIO line 4 (BCM, physical pin 7) every 100 ms. It reads the sensor, which drives the line LOW when an object is within the calibrated range and HIGH otherwise. When a detection occurs, it writes a timestamped entry to a file named `proximity.log` using an ISO 8601 UTC format. It also blinks an LED attached to GPIO line 17 (BCM, physical pin 11) by turning it on for 100 ms and then off. The program handles errors, checks the return status of every driver call, and releases the GPIO lines and closes the chip on any exit path, including receipt of SIGINT or SIGTERM.

