This C program initializes the I2C bus and GPIO, reads the distance from a TDK InvenSense ICU-20201 ultrasonic Time-of-Flight sensor every 100 ms, and logs each distance reading together with an ISO-8601 timestamp to a file named `distance_log.txt`. The LED connected to GPIO 17 (BCM numbering) is turned on when the measured distance is below 20 cm and off otherwise. The program handles cases where the sensor is absent or the bus reports errors in a graceful manner, and ensures that all resources—including the I2C handle, the GPIO pin, and any driver state—are cleanly released on every exit path by handling SIGINT and SIGTERM signals.

