This C program uses the `libgpiod` library to handle GPIO operations and interrupts on a Raspberry Pi 3 Model B+. It sets up an interrupt-driven parking sensor using an HC-SR04 ultrasonic sensor and a buzzer. The program measures the distance to an object in front of the sensor every 100 ms and outputs the distance to the console. If the distance is less than 30 cm, the buzzer is activated; otherwise, it is turned off. The program handles timeouts and invalid readings, and it ensures a clean shutdown on SIGINT.

