This C program initializes a Raspberry Pi Zero W to control a gate using a VL53L1X time-of-flight sensor on I2C bus 1 and an SG90 servo driven from GPIO18 (BCM) with hardware PWM. It logs every event with a timestamp to a file named `gate_log.txt`. The program performs full bare-metal I2C initialization for the VL53L1X including a software reset, waits for boot, starts ranging and reads the 16-bit distance, automatically opens the gate when an object is detected within 20 cm and closes it when the path is clear. It handles I2C communication errors and sensor-absent conditions gracefully with retry logic, responds to remote-control commands via the driver’s v2 callback API using the calls `force_open`, `force_close` and `status_request`, and ensures that all resources are cleanly released on every exit path by installing appropriate signal handlers.

