This C program initializes a VL53L1X time-of-flight sensor on I2C bus 1, configures it, and continuously polls for distance measurements. It opens the gate when an object is detected within 20 cm and closes it otherwise. The program logs each event with an ISO 8601 UTC timestamp to a file named `gate_events.log`. It handles sensor-absent or bus-error conditions by logging the error and exiting gracefully. The program also implements SIGINT/SIGTERM signal handling to ensure proper cleanup on exit.

