This C program sets up a Raspberry Pi 4 Model B to detect proximity using an MPR121 capacitive touch sensor connected on I2C bus 1. It reads the device ID to verify the sensor is present, configures the MPR121 registers, monitors the touch inputs for a proximity event, and logs the event with a timestamp to a file named `proximity.log`. The program handles I2C communication errors gracefully and ensures that all resources are cleanly released when the program receives a SIGINT or SIGTERM signal.

