This C program interfaces with a Silicon Labs Si1182‑A‑GM optical sensor over I2C using the /dev/i2c‑1 device. It verifies the sensor by reading its part ID register and configures the measurement rate register to the documented values. The program continuously reads ambient light (lux) and proximity data every 100 ms, logging each timestamped reading to a CSV line in a file named `biometric_log.txt` and printing the same line to stdout. It includes SIGINT and SIGTERM handlers that close the I2C file descriptor and the log file, releasing all resources on normal and error exits.

