This C program interfaces with a Sensirion SHT40 humidity and temperature sensor over I2C bus 1 using the SDA pin on GPIO2 (BCM) and the SCL pin on GPIO3 (BCM) at the documented 7-bit address. It issues the high-repeatability measurement command, waits for the measurement to complete, reads the 6-byte result, validates each reading with the Sensirion CRC-8 algorithm, and logs timestamped temperature and humidity values to a file named `sht40_log.txt` every 5 seconds. The program robustly handles errors from opening the I2C device, ioctl calls, writes, and reads by logging an error and retrying on the next cycle, and it cleanly closes both the I2C file descriptor and the log file when receiving SIGINT or SIGTERM.

