This C program reads temperature from an Analog Devices TMP05 digital temperature sensor connected to GPIO4 on a Raspberry Pi 4 Model B. It uses the `libgpiod` library to handle GPIO operations and timestamps. The program logs each valid temperature reading along with an ISO-8601 timestamp to a file named "temperature_log.txt". It also handles SIGINT and SIGTERM signals to perform a clean shutdown. The program checks for valid temperature readings and logs any failures, with a maximum of three consecutive failures before logging a "SENSOR MALFUNCTION" entry.

