This C program reads temperature and humidity from an Adafruit SHT40 sensor on the I2C bus using the `libgpiod` library. It waits at least 8.5 ms after each command for conversion and sampling, reads exactly six bytes (two bytes of temperature followed by one CRC byte, then two bytes of humidity followed by one CRC byte), validates both CRC-8 values using the documented polynomial and initial value, and appends a line containing a timestamp and the measured values to a file named `environmental_data.txt`, flushing the file after each write. It checks for errors at every stage including driver library initialization, opening the I2C interface, I2C write and read operations, CRC validation, and all file operations, and it installs a SIGINT handler that cleanly closes the I2C handle, terminates the driver library, and closes the log file before exiting.

