This C program continuously monitors air-duct pressure in a simulated HVAC system using the Sensirion SDP810-500Pa differential pressure sensor on the I2C bus. It triggers a measurement, waits at least 50 ms, then reads the 9-byte result (2 bytes pressure, 1 byte CRC, 2 bytes temperature, 1 byte CRC, 3 bytes scale factor) once per second, validating every I2C read and write as well as each CRC-8 using the polynomial and initial value documented for the sensor. It logs each successful sample to a file named `hvac_pressure_log.txt` in CSV format with columns timestamp, pressure_Pa, temperature_C, and on any I2C or CRC error writing an error line with the timestamp and continuing. It handles SIGINT (Ctrl+C) by closing the I2C handle, flushing and closing the log file, and calling the library's cleanup API function before terminating.

