This C program uses the `libscd4x` library to interact with the Sensirion SCD40 CO2 sensor over I2C. It buffers the sensor readings in a thread-safe circular buffer and periodically persists the data to a CSV file. The program also handles errors and logs them to a separate file. The main loop waits at least one second after issuing the start-periodic-measurement command before the first read, and it reads the sensor every five seconds. The program uses a separate logging thread to write the buffered records to the CSV file every sixty seconds. The program handles SIGINT by using a volatile sig_atomic_t running flag to stop the main loop, send the documented stop-periodic-measurement command, join the logging thread, flush any remaining buffered data to a final CSV file, close the I2C handle, and cleanly terminate the driver without any resource leaks.

