This C program reads ambient and object temperatures from a Melexis MLX90614ESF-BAA infrared temperature sensor connected to a Raspberry Pi Zero W via the I2C bus. It logs the timestamped readings to a file named `temperature_log.txt` every 2 seconds. The program controls a cooling fan connected to GPIO18 (BCM) with hysteresis, turning it on when the object temperature exceeds 30°C and turning it off when it falls below 28°C. The program handles SIGINT and SIGTERM by closing the I2C handle, turning off the fan, and terminating the driver library. It validates driver library initialization, opening the I2C bus, and each I2C read/write operation, retrying any failed read up to three times with a 10ms delay between attempts and skipping logging for invalid readings.

