This C program continuously monitors a YL-83 rain sensor connected to GPIO17 (active-low) via the GPIO bus, polling the sensor every 2 seconds. When rain is detected, it commands an L298N motor driver to close a window by driving the motor forward for exactly 5 seconds using ENA on GPIO22, IN1 on GPIO23, and IN2 on GPIO24, then stops the motor. Each detection, motor start, motor stop, and any error condition is logged to stdout with a timestamp. The program checks the return status of every driver call and explicitly handles the situation where the GPIO chip cannot be opened. It also installs SIGINT and SIGTERM handlers so that on program termination the motor is safely stopped and all GPIO lines are released.

