This C program initializes a PWM-driven cooling fan on a Raspberry Pi 4 Model B using the MAX31855 thermocouple amplifier connected on SPI0. It reads the temperature every second, computes the duty cycle based on a piecewise fan curve, and stores the timestamp, temperature, and duty cycle in a circular buffer. The program handles errors and signals, and prints the full contents of the buffer on SIGINT.

