This C program uses the `libgpiod` library to monitor a magnetic rotary encoder connected to the Raspberry Pi 4 Model B. The encoder is configured with two TMAG5110A1 Hall-effect latch sensors, one connected to GPIO17 (Channel A) and the other to GPIO18 (Channel B). The program sets up the GPIO pins as open-drain outputs with internal pull-up resistors enabled. It implements a 2-bit quadrature state machine to resolve 360 pulses per revolution into a normalized angular position ranging from 0.00 to 360.00 degrees. Each timestamped position change is logged to a file named `encoder_log.txt`. The program handles errors for both GPIO initialization and file I/O operations and ensures that all resources are cleanly released when the program receives a SIGINT or SIGTERM signal.

