This C program reads flow rates from two Sensirion SLF3S‑0600F Liquid Flow Sensors connected on I2C (/dev/i2c‑1) and logs the average flow rate to a file named `flow_log.txt` every second. It also drives an alarm on GPIO17 (BCM) when the average of the valid sensor readings falls below 0.5 ml/min and keeps the alarm low otherwise. The program handles a clean shutdown on SIGINT or SIGTERM by releasing the GPIO line, closing the I2C file descriptor and the log file.

