This C program uses the `libgpiod` library to monitor two E18-D80NK IR obstacle sensors connected to GPIO pins 17 and 18 on a Raspberry Pi 4 Model B. It continuously checks the state of the sensors and records a timestamped entry in a file named `stall_log.txt` whenever both sensors detect an obstacle (i.e., read LOW) for at least 2 seconds, ensuring that each stall event is recorded only once. The program handles file I/O errors and gracefully exits when interrupted by a SIGINT or SIGTERM signal.

