This C program interfaces with the Texas Instruments TMAG5170-Q1 I2C 3D Hall-effect sensor on I2C bus 1, configures it for continuous-conversion mode with all three axes enabled and a 50 mT range, reads the X, Y, and Z magnetic field values every 100 ms in an infinite loop until the user terminates the program with Ctrl-C, logging each reading to a CSV file named `magnetic_log.csv` with an ISO-8601 timestamp and writing a header row if the file is newly created. It checks every I2C read and write return code and handles sensor-absent or bus-error conditions by printing error messages to stderr and continuing operation. Finally, it registers a SIGINT/SIGTERM handler that cleanly releases resources by closing the I2C handle, closing the CSV file, and invoking the sensor's library cleanup call before exiting.

