This C program uses the `libgpiod` library to interact with the Raspberry Pi's GPIO bus. It initializes four Keywish KY-032 sensors and an LED, and continuously polls the sensors to determine if any object is detected. If any sensor detects an object, the LED is turned on; otherwise, it is turned off. The program handles GPIO initialization errors and cleanly releases all resources when receiving a SIGINT or SIGTERM.

