This C program initializes the Raspberry Pi Zero W to monitor the coolant flow rate from a Sensirion SLF3S‑1300F Liquid Flow Sensor connected to I2C bus 1. It continuously reads the sensor data, validates the CRC, and logs the results to a CSV file. The program handles I2C read failures and CRC errors by attempting to recover by re-initializing the I2C handle. It also handles SIGINT to perform a graceful shutdown.

