This C program implements a flame detection safety system using the Keyes KY-026 Flame Sensor and an active buzzer on a Raspberry Pi 3 Model B+. It polls the sensor every 500 ms, breaking the 2-second buzzer activation and the 500 ms poll interval into 100 ms slices to ensure it can respond promptly to shutdown signals. It logs a timestamped "FLAME DETECTED" entry to a file named `alert_log.txt` when a flame is detected, drives the buzzer HIGH for 2 seconds, and ensures that only the transition triggers logging and buzzing. The program includes signal handling for SIGINT and SIGTERM, checks every driver library call, file operation, and system call for failure, and exits cleanly with code 0 on clean shutdown.

