This C program uses the `libgpiod` library to monitor a Keyes KY-026 Flame Sensor connected to GPIO17 on a Raspberry Pi 3 Model B+. It sets up a signal handler to handle SIGINT and SIGTERM signals, opens the GPIO chip and line, requests the line as an input with an internal pull-up, and enters a loop to poll the line for falling edges. When a falling edge is detected, it prints a timestamped alert to the console and appends it to a log file. The program handles errors and ensures that resources are released on all exit paths.

