This C program uses the `libgpiod` library to monitor two Omron D7E-5 tilt sensors connected to the GPIO bus on a Raspberry Pi 5. It configures the lines as inputs with active-low pull-up, polls them every 100 ms, and uses a 50 ms debounce window to detect edges. It logs only transitions from inactive (1) to active (0) to `/var/log/tilt_events.log` in the specified format. The program handles chip open failure, line request failure, and read errors by printing an error message to stderr and either exiting or continuing gracefully as appropriate. It also installs handlers for SIGINT and SIGTERM that release all driver resources and close the log file cleanly before exiting.

