This C program initializes the Raspberry Pi 4 Model B to communicate with a TCS34725 color sensor using the I2C bus. It powers on the sensor, enables RGBC mode, sets the integration time to approximately 154ms, and enters a loop to read and print the calibrated red, green, blue, and clear values. It also controls an LED connected to GPIO pin 17 based on the calibrated red value exceeding a threshold of 200. The program handles SIGINT and SIGTERM signals and ensures that all resources are released on exit.

