This C program reads ambient light and color data from an ADPD188BI sensor on I2C bus 1, samples the sensor every 500 ms, combines the ALS LSB and MSB into a 16-bit unsigned value, and logs each timestamped reading of ALS, red, green, and blue channels to a CSV file named `color_log.csv` with a header row. It also controls an LED connected to GPIO18 (BCM) using hardware PWM so that brighter ambient light increases the LED brightness. The program handles I2C errors, signal handling for SIGINT and SIGTERM, and performs a graceful shutdown that closes the I2C handle, turns off the LED, and closes the CSV file.

