This C program initializes the Raspberry Pi 4 Model B to communicate with an Analog Devices ADIS16448 IMU over SPI bus 0 using chip-select CS0 on GPIO8 (BCM) in SPI mode 3 with a maximum clock of 1 MHz. It reads the gyroscope and accelerometer registers using the single-register read protocol, applies the gyro scale of 0.02 dps/LSB and accel scale of 0.00025 g/LSB, and logs the six values (gyroscope X, Y, Z and accelerometer X, Y, Z) to the console every 100 ms. The program includes robust error handling for SPI initialization, ioctl transfers, and data reads, and handles SIGINT and SIGTERM to cleanly release resources by closing the SPI device file and the driver library chip before exiting.

