This C program continuously polls an Adafruit ADXL345 accelerometer on I2C bus 1 every 10 ms in full-resolution mode with a ±2 g range. It checks the device ID register, verifies the result of every I2C read or write, and when the computed total acceleration magnitude exceeds a 2.5 g threshold, it turns on a red LED connected to GPIO 17 (BCM) for 500 ms, records the event to a file named `impact_log.txt` with a timestamp and the magnitude together with the X, Y, and Z components. It ensures that on normal exit or on receipt of SIGINT or SIGTERM all resources—including the I2C handle, the LED GPIO, the log file, and any driver state—are cleanly released, while also handling sensor-absent and bus-error conditions according to the verification steps.

