This C program continuously polls a GY-45 MMA8452Q 3-axis accelerometer on I2C bus `/dev/i2c-1` at roughly 100 Hz. It verifies the sensor identity, initializes the device, reads the six data registers in a single block, computes the absolute tilt, and logs entries to `fall_log.txt` when a tilt exceeding 45 degrees is detected. The program handles errors, uses a signal handler for cleanup, and releases resources on all exit paths.

