This C program controls two 12V electromagnetic door locks using TIP120-driven 5V active-HIGH relay modules on the Raspberry Pi 4 Model B. It initializes the GPIO pins, generates a random six-digit security code, prompts the user for input, compares the input with the generated code, logs access to a file, and unlocks the doors for 5 seconds on a match. The program handles errors, installs a SIGINT/SIGTERM handler, and ensures proper cleanup on exit.

