This C program initializes the I2C bus and address for the HMC5883L magnetometer, reads the initial offsets, and then continuously reads raw magnetic field data. It calculates a running average of the last 100 samples to compute hard-iron offsets, applies those offsets to each new raw reading, and prints the offset-corrected X, Y, and Z components to stdout every 500 ms. The program handles I2C read or write errors by printing an error message to stderr and continues running. It also cleanly releases the I2C handle and any driver resources when it receives SIGINT or SIGTERM.

