This C program uses the `libgpiod` library to control the GPIO pins on a Raspberry Pi 3 Model B+. It sets up two solenoids connected to GPIO17 and GPIO27, alternately energizing them with a 500 ms delay. The program includes a signal handler to cleanly exit on Ctrl+C, releasing the GPIO lines and closing the chip.

