This C program implements a dual-factor door-lock authentication scheme using two UART ports and two active-HIGH relay modules driving 12-V electromagnetic door locks. The program reads 6-digit codes from `/dev/serial0` and `/dev/serial1` at 9600 baud, 8N1 framing, with a 5-second per-port read timeout and non-blocking reads. It checks if both received codes match each other and the constant expected code "123456" using a constant-time string comparison. If the codes match, it drives both relay GPIOs HIGH for exactly 2 seconds and then sets them LOW. The program handles errors and installs handlers for SIGINT and SIGTERM to perform a clean shutdown.

