This C program implements a smart irrigation system for a Raspberry Pi Zero W. It uses the `libgpiod` library to control GPIO pins and the `rand()` function to simulate soil moisture values. The program logs each irrigation event to a file and handles signals to deactivate all relays and clean up resources.

