This C program initializes a VL53L1X time-of-flight sensor connected to I2C bus 1 on a Raspberry Pi 4 Model B. It continuously reads the distance from the sensor every 100 ms, prints the distance to stdout, and drives a relay connected to GPIO18 (BCM) so that the relay is set HIGH when the measured distance is less than or equal to 50 cm and LOW otherwise. The program handles errors by logging them to stderr and ensures that on receipt of SIGINT, it cleanly releases all resources by closing the I2C interface, setting the relay pin low, and terminating the driver usage.

