This C program implements an automated plant watering system using four 5V relay modules connected to GPIO17, GPIO18, GPIO27, and GPIO22 on a Raspberry Pi 4 Model B. The program opens the GPIO library, requests the lines as outputs with active-low semantics, sets them HIGH at startup, and then in a main loop activates each relay in turn for exactly 5 seconds, repeating the whole sequence every 24 hours. The start time of each full cycle is logged to a file named `watering_log.txt`. The program handles errors and releases all resources on all exit paths, including the case where the GPIO chip cannot be opened.

