This C program sets up an audio capture device using ALSA, computes the RMS amplitude of each buffer, and maps that amplitude to a color on an RGB LED using software PWM. It handles buffer overruns and suspended states, and simulates audio input if ALSA is not available. The program also includes signal handlers for SIGINT and SIGTERM to cleanly release resources.

