This C program reads calibrated color values from a TCS34725 color sensor connected on I2C bus 1 at the documented address, samples the sensor every 500 ms using the driver library's timing call while configuring the sensor for a 154 ms integration time, and logs each reading to a file named `color_data.csv` with a header row followed by lines containing the Unix-epoch timestamp and the C, R, G, B values as comma-separated fields. The program checks every I2C open, write, and read operation, and on any failure prints an error message to stderr, records zeros for the sensor values for that cycle, and continues running without crashing. It also registers SIGINT and SIGTERM handlers that cleanly close the I2C handle, close the CSV file, and terminate the driver library before exiting.

