This C program initializes a smart greenhouse irrigation system using a simulated moisture sensor and four SainSmart 5V relay modules connected to the GPIO bus on a Raspberry Pi 4 Model B. The program reads a random moisture value every 5 seconds, activates or deactivates the corresponding relay based on the moisture level, and logs the sensor reading, relay state, and timestamp to a file named `irrigation_log.txt`. The program handles errors and installs a signal handler to ensure proper cleanup on exit.

