This C program continuously reads acceleration data from an Analog Devices ADXL345 accelerometer on the I2C bus using the documented address, polls the sensor every 100 ms, and detects a free‑fall event when the absolute value of the x, y, and z readings are all below 0.2 g for a continuous 0.5 second period confirmed by a second reading after a 0.5 second delay. When such an event is confirmed, the program sets GPIO27 (BCM numbering) high to trigger an alarm that remains asserted for 5 seconds, logs each confirmed free‑fall occurrence to a file named freefall.log in CSV format with a timestamp in “YYYY‑MM‑DD HH:MM:SS” and the three axis values to three decimal places, handle any I2C communication errors by printing a diagnostic message to stderr and then continuing operation while checking the result of every driver and I2C call, and install a SIGINT handler that cleanly closes the I2C handle, drives the alarm GPIO low, and shuts down the driver before exiting.

