This C program uses the `libgpiod` library to interact with the Raspberry Pi's GPIO pins. It sets up an interrupt-driven system to measure the distance using an HC-SR04 ultrasonic sensor. The program logs each valid reading to a file named `distance_log.txt` in CSV format. It handles errors, such as driver library initialization failure, file open failure, invalid pulse widths, and sensor timeouts. The program also includes a SIGINT handler to gracefully terminate the program on interruption.

