This C program uses the `libgpiod` library to control a hobby servo connected to GPIO pin 18 on a Raspberry Pi. It also includes two momentary push-buttons connected to GPIO pins 21 and 22, with pull-up resistors enabled. The program polls the buttons in a tight loop, implements debouncing, and sends pulse widths to the servo to lock and unlock it. It outputs status messages to stdout and handles errors gracefully. The program also installs a SIGINT/SIGTERM handler to stop the servo and exit cleanly.

