This C program uses the `libgpiod` library to interact with the Raspberry Pi's GPIO bus. It reads a TTP223 capacitive touch sensor on BCM GPIO4 and drives a 5 V active-HIGH relay on BCM GPIO17. The program polls the sensor every 50 ms and toggles the relay state on each rising edge of the touch. If the sensor remains continuously HIGH for more than 10 seconds, the program forces the relay OFF and ignores further toggles until the sensor is released. The program also includes a SIGINT/SIGTERM handler to set a volatile flag so the main loop can exit cleanly, after which the program releases the relay and calls the library's API call() for cleanup.

