This C program implements closed-loop proportional solenoid valve flow control using an ASCO RedHat 8210 series proportional solenoid valve and a YF-S201 flow sensor on a Raspberry Pi 4 Model B. The program uses the libgpiod library for GPIO operations and the pigpio library for PWM and interrupt handling. The valve PWM is generated on GPIO 18 (BCM, hardware PWM 0), the valve enable/direction line on GPIO 23 (BCM, active-high), and the flow sensor is connected to GPIO 24 (BCM) with an interrupt on each rising edge. The program logs the flow rate and valve position to a local file named flow_log.csv every 100 ms, applying a proportional controller with Kp = 1.0 to compute a PWM duty cycle in the range 0-255 based on a target flow rate supplied as a command-line argument. The program handles SIGINT and SIGTERM to perform a graceful shutdown that sets the PWM duty cycle to zero, drives GPIO 23 low, closes the CSV file, and cleanly terminates the driver library.

