This C program initializes the I2C bus and GPIO lines for communication with an MPR121 capacitive touch sensor. It sets up the sensor in stop mode, configures touch and release thresholds, filter, charge time, and electrode current, and then switches the device into run mode. The program continuously monitors the touch status and toggles a relay connected to GPIO17 whenever any electrode reports a touch. It handles errors and signals for graceful shutdown.

