This C program continuously monitors a weight-triggered solenoid lock using a load cell amplified by an HX711 on the GPIO bus. It reads the HX711 sensor every 500ms, enforces a read timeout of 0.5 seconds, and logs each reading with a timestamp to `weight_log.txt`. It also performs a one-time startup calibration by averaging 100 readings at zero load to determine the offset. The program computes weight using the loaded or default scale and offset, engages the solenoid when the computed weight exceeds a calibrated threshold of 10.0 kg, and handles SIGINT to cleanly shut down by releasing all GPIO resources and closing open files.

