This C program continuously monitors a Seeed Studio Grove Rain Sensor connected to GPIO4 on the Raspberry Pi 4 Model B. It debounces the sensor readings by taking five readings spaced 50 ms apart and declares rain when at least three of those readings are LOW. When rain is detected, it drives a DC motor through an L298N motor driver using IN1 on GPIO17, IN2 on GPIO18, and the PWM enable line on GPIO27. The motor is set to close the window for exactly five seconds with a 1000 Hz PWM signal and a duty cycle value of 150. The program logs each rain event and each motor action with timestamps to `/var/log/window_control.log` via syslog. It checks the sensor only once every 60 seconds and waits an additional 60 seconds after a closing operation before the next check. The program handles any GPIO initialization failures with clear error messages and distinct exit codes, provides robust error handling for all sensor reads and motor control actions, and ensures that on receipt of SIGINT or SIGTERM the motor is stopped, all GPIO resources are released, and the log file is properly closed for a graceful shutdown.

