This C program continuously monitors a kitchen ingredient stock level using a TAL220B load cell amplified by an HX711 connected on the GPIO bus with bit-banged communication. It reads the weight once every second, checks if the measured weight falls below 100 g, and if so, activates a solenoid lock attached to GPIO17 (BCM) for exactly five seconds. Each weight check, lock activation, and any error condition are logged with a timestamp to a file named `stock_events.txt`. The program implements robust error handling for all reads, writes, and file operations and performs proper resource cleanup when receiving SIGINT or SIGTERM.

