This C program controls a line-following robot using a Keywish 3-Way Infrared Tracking Sensor and two DC motors driven through an L298N motor driver. The program reads sensor states every 10 ms and adjusts motor speeds based on the sensor readings. The control law ensures that the robot drives straight when the middle sensor is low, turns right when only the left sensor is low, turns left when only the right sensor is low, and stops when no sensor is low. The program logs sensor states and motor speeds to a file named `trace_log.txt` with an ISO 8601 timestamp. The program includes robust error handling for initializing the driver library, opening the log file, and all GPIO operations, and a SIGINT handler that stops both motors, closes the log file, terminates the driver library, and ensures that all driver library API calls are properly released before exiting.

