This C program uses the `libgpiod` library to control a servo motor connected to GPIO18 on a Raspberry Pi. It also includes two push-buttons connected to GPIO21 and GPIO22 for locking and unlocking, respectively. The program debounces each button press with a 100 ms delay and sets the servo pulse width to 1000 µs (≈0°) for locking and 2000 µs (≈180°) for unlocking, respecting the API's safe pulse-width range of 500-2500 µs. The program handles initialization failures gracefully by printing an error message and exits cleanly on receiving a SIGINT signal.

