This C program reads ambient light from four BH1750FVI sensors attached to I2C-1, waits 180 ms after each start-conversion command, and repeats this acquisition loop once per second. It handles any open, address-set, write, read, or partial-read failure by inserting a NaN value for that sensor while continuing with the others. After gathering the lux values, it broadcasts a UDP multicast packet to 239.255.255.250:5005 containing a semicolon-separated list of sensor_id,lux pairs. It also installs handlers for SIGINT and SIGTERM that set a termination flag so the loop can exit cleanly, ensuring that all file descriptors for I2C and the UDP socket are closed on every exit path.

