This C program sets up a UART connection to a Texas Instruments AWR1642 mmWave radar sensor and reads range detection data. It uses the `libgpiod` library to handle GPIO pins for UART communication. The program reads data in non-canonical mode, accumulates partial reads into a line buffer, and parses complete newline-terminated ASCII lines. It handles sensor-absent or bus-error conditions using a select call with a 2-second timeout. The program also installs signal handlers for SIGINT and SIGTERM to ensure a graceful shutdown.

