This C program initializes the GPIO pins for the Keywish 3‑Way Tracking Sensor and the UART device, reads the sensor states at 10 Hz, and logs them to the console. If all sensors detect an obstacle, it sends an emergency stop message over the UART device. The program handles errors and exits gracefully, including closing the UART port, terminating the driver library, and releasing all resources.
